<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=tide-mill">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tide mill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A tide mill is a water mill driven by the rise and fall of the tide, which fills a mill pond through a one-way gate and releases the water to turn a wheel. Finds on the Irish coast have pushed back the date of the earliest ones: a 6th-century vertical-wheeled mill at Killoteran near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a>, a twin-flume mill of about 630 on Little Island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a>, and a mill of 619 at Nendrum in Strangford Lough. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> a mill of 691–692 was excavated at Ebbsfleet, and eight are listed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domesday-book">Domesday Book</a> of 1086.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tide-mill.jpg" alt="Tide mill" width="330" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marc Ryckaert (MJJR) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olhao_Tide_Mill.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>6th century</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Killoteran, near Waterford, Ireland</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>A tide mill on the River Fleet in London may date to Roman times and is possibly the earliest in the Roman world.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/water-wheel">Water wheel<span>4th century BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=tide-mill">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
